Z||000000||Monkeyman||12-10-1999||02:18 PM||||There is an '84 Indy for sale on eBay.  The text suggests that someone could cut it up and use it for a donor car for a kit.  This looks like it's in good condition.  I'd hate for someone to cut up an Indy since there weren't many made.  I emailed the seller and explained this to him, but I'm sure it doesn't matter.  All he wants is to sell the car.  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=216664239" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=216664239</A> <BR>It's going for $2500.  If I had the money, I'd bid on it just so I knew that it was going to a good home.||||reg||4
Z||000001||batboy||12-10-1999||10:20 PM||||OMG! I want those wheels! Been looking around for a set of wheels that I liked, but haven't really seen anything I've liked much. But like those, I wonder if you can still get them. I'm guessing they're aftermarket, right?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||12-10-1999||11:18 PM||||Personally, I think those wheels look generic, but to each his own!  At least they look like the ones on the "real" Indys.  I guess that's the look they were going for.  I like the ones on 87FieroGTs car.  (I think I've got the right name with the right car?!)||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||12-10-1999||11:26 PM||||For the condition of that car, the wear on the steering wheel seems very excessive.  It had to have come from another car.<BR>I also do not care for those wheels, I prefer the stock white Indy Fiero wheels. But, everyone is entitled to their opinions.||||reg||4
Z||000004||fierospeeder||12-10-1999||11:44 PM||||I also noticed the indy pace car because of my addiction to ebay.  There is wear in the interior, and if you look closely the seats seem worn also.  If i wanted a rare indy pace car, i would skip this one, seems like it was a daily driver.  I seem very few selling these and i would get someone that never drove it and kept it garaged.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-11-1999||12:06 AM||||I'm not sure if the price will be right on it or not.  I just thought somebody might be interested.  Also, I didn't like the thought of somebody using this car for a kit car donor.  No matter what shape it's in, it's still one of the rarer Fieros.  And with the 4 cyl, I can think of lots of other Fieros that would make much better donors.  I think there was an old thread that went something like this.  Someone was gonna use an '88 GT for a donor and it was suggested that he leave the GT alone and find a Formula.  Same difference.<P>Batboy-I tried to find out what the name of the wheel is, but I'm not having any luck so far.  I emailed an aftermarket wheel store with a pic of the car/wheel.  Hopefully they can identify it and let me know if it's still available and the price.  I'll let you know.<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 12-11-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||12-11-1999||01:10 AM||||Wheel styles are a personal preference, so I don't mind if people don't care for that look, just as I don't want any of the hundreds of variants of the "spoked" style wheels that everyone seems to have nowadays. <BR>I'm not interested in putting those wheels (the ones in the pic) on an Indy Fiero, but rather on my ol' 85 SE Batmobile. If I had an Indy car, I'd want to restore it back to original, but again, that's my own personal preference.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-11-1999||01:42 AM||||I understand.  Personally, I like a "solid" syle wheel, but I don't know if one would look good on a Fiero with such a big offset.  Ever seen the old "Torq Thrust D"s?  I think they used to be on some of the old Camaros. I know they're the spoke wheels you don't like, but they might look good on the batmobile.  BTW--I saw a Fiero the other day on the way to OH with VERY wide spoked wheels.  Looked like sh**!!  Here's a pic of the Torq Thrust Ds: <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TorqThrustD.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 12-11-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||12-11-1999||09:22 AM||||Hey, that almost looks like the old Cragars my brother used to have on his 69 Olds 442. It's not that I don't like the spoked style wheels, actually I do really like the looks of a number of them. I just don't want to put them on my car. I want to be different.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||12-11-1999||10:28 AM||||Batboy... I used to have a set of wheels *exactly* like that on my 85 GT. (I was also after the "pace car" look.) They were made by Progressive (not sure what they were called), and came from NTW. Happy hunting.||||reg||1
